<title>SWITZERLAND: Asia/Far East heads Swiss cargo Oct 1 rate hike.</title>
<headline>Asia/Far East heads Swiss cargo Oct 1 rate hike.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Cargo, the cargo arm of Swissair, said the Asia/Far East zone would attract the biggest increases in its ex-Switzerland rates, effective October 1.</p>
<p>Rises of eight percent would be applied to ex-Switzerland cargo destined for Bangkok, Hong Kong, Singapore and Taipei, Swiss Cargo added.</p>
<p>Other Asia/Far East destinations, notably Bombay, Delhi and Manila would increase by five to six percent while three percent rises were planned for Beijing, Shanghai, Seoul and Tokyo and Osaka.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, in the Middle East and Africa zones, Swiss Cargo s ex-Switzerland rates would be unchanged with the exception of Johannesburg and Cape Town where tariffs were set to fall by five percent. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
